                <pb facs="0224" n="116" xml:id="pg116"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-01-29"><hi rendition="#italic">January 29, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received January 29.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson reports that at an interview in which interference with the coal
                    trade of British subjects was discussed, the representative of Great Britain,
                    whose views are shared by his Belgian, French, Italian, and Portuguese
                    colleagues, declared that all other means would be exhausted before force would
                    be resorted to and intimated that recognition might be recommended by him.</p>
            </div>
